<?php
/**
 * Themeasy Elementor Widget: Table of Contents
 *
 * Auto-generated table of contents: the client-side module scans the page (or
 * a custom container) for the chosen heading levels, assigns stable anchor ids
 * and builds a nested, numbered/bulleted link list. A scrollspy highlights the
 * section being read and slides an accent indicator along the rail, an
 * optional hairline under the header fills with reading progress, clicks
 * smooth-scroll with a sticky-header offset, and the box can collapse and/or
 * stick inside its column. The list itself is generated by JavaScript (the
 * page markup is only known in the browser): with no JS the widget renders
 * its shell and the empty list collapses; when fewer headings than the
 * configured minimum are found the whole widget hides. In the editor preview
 * (--static) the list is rebuilt from the preview document on every render
 * while scrollspy, smooth scroll and collapse stay inert. Reduced motion
 * disables the indicator/progress/collapse transitions and smooth scrolling.
 *
 * @package Themeasy
 * @since 1.0.0
 */

